        "node_id": "n_1_bc23f8",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1 (revised): Ensure that the placement of ones in the matrix respects the symmetry requirement and that the total number of ones placed equals k. For a symmetric matrix, each position above the diagonal determines the value below it, so we need exactly k ones to be placed in such a way that they satisfy this property. If k exceeds the maximum possible number of ones that can fit into the matrix while maintaining symmetry, return -1.",
